// Generated by `apollo features sync` from apollo/features.json. Do not edit.

// The bundle rules are not here. They arrive with the grants, in the same
// `Client.getModuleSettings()` response, as `catalog[key].requires` — one
// list with one meaning, read at the moment it is needed. A generated copy
// was a second answer to the same question: the two diverged on 2026-09-10,
// when the catalog required Post for Live and Poll and this file still had
// both standalone, and the shape of the copy invited the other error as
// well — it carried `all` and `any` side by side while the catalog has one
// `requires` meaning any, so a reader mapped it onto whichever name they
// assumed.
//
// What this costs: before the first response lands, and if core cannot be
// reached, there are no rules to apply and no module cascades. That is the
// honest answer rather than a guess — the rules are the network's, and a
// client that invented them would be withholding a feature on its own
// authority.

